### Signup with File Upload Documentation
### This file demonstrates the complete flow for user signup with file uploads (profile picture and identity picture)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@contentType = application/json

### ============================================
### STEP 1: Get Upload URL for Profile Picture
### ============================================
### Request a signed URL to upload the profile picture
### Purpose must be "profile" for profile pictures

POST {{baseUrl}}/s3/upload-url
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fileName": "profile-picture.jpg",
  "fileType": "image",
  "filePurpose": "profile"
}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "data": {
###     "uploadUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/profile/...",
###     "file": {
###       "id": "uuid-here",
###       "fileName": "profile-picture.jpg",
###       "fileType": "image",
###       "filePurpose": "profile",
###       "url": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/profile/...",
###       ...
###     },
###     "uploadToken": "token-string-here"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### STEP 2: Upload Profile Picture to S3
### ============================================
### Use the uploadUrl from Step 1 to upload the actual file
### This is a PUT request to the signed URL (not to our API)
### Note: Replace {{uploadUrl}} with the actual URL from Step 1 response

PUT {{uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./path/to/your/profile-picture.jpg

### ============================================
### STEP 3: Get Upload URL for Identity Picture
### ============================================
### Request a signed URL to upload the identity picture
### Purpose must be "identity" for identity verification documents

POST {{baseUrl}}/s3/upload-url
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fileName": "identity-front.jpg",
  "fileType": "image",
  "filePurpose": "identity"
}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "data": {
###     "uploadUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/identity/...",
###     "file": {
###       "id": "uuid-here",
###       "fileName": "identity-front.jpg",
###       "fileType": "image",
###       "filePurpose": "identity",
###       "url": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/identity/...",
###       ...
###     },
###     "uploadToken": "token-string-here"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### STEP 4: Upload Identity Picture to S3
### ============================================
### Use the uploadUrl from Step 3 to upload the actual file
### Note: Replace {{uploadUrl}} with the actual URL from Step 3 response

PUT {{uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./path/to/your/identity-front.jpg

### ============================================
### STEP 5: Register as Client with File Uploads
### ============================================
### After uploading files to S3, use the fileId, uploadToken, and purpose from Steps 1 and 3
### IMPORTANT: Both profilePicture and identityPicture must be arrays, even for single files
### Note: profilePicture is optional, identityPicture is required

POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register/client
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "phone": "+1234567890",
  "country": "United States",
  "jobTitle": "Software Engineer",
  "overview": "Experienced software engineer with 5+ years in web development",
  "profilePicture": [
    {
      "fileId": "uuid-from-step-1-file-id",
      "token": "token-from-step-1-upload-token",
      "purpose": "profile"
    }
  ],
  "identityPicture": [
    {
      "fileId": "uuid-from-step-3-file-id",
      "token": "token-from-step-3-upload-token",
      "purpose": "identity"
    }
  ]
}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Client registered successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "user": {
###       "id": "user-uuid",
###       "name": "John Doe",
###       "country": "United States",
###       "jobTitle": "Software Engineer",
###       "overview": "Experienced software engineer with 5+ years in web development",
###       "phone": "+1234567890",
###       "mode": "client",
###       "profilePicture": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/profile/...",
###       "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###     },
###     "wallet": {
###       "id": "wallet-uuid",
###       "userId": "user-uuid",
###       "balance": 0,
###       "currency": "USD"
###     },
###     "identity": {
###       "id": "identity-uuid",
###       "userId": "user-uuid",
###       "isVerified": false,
###       "images": ["https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/identity/..."]
###     }
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### STEP 6: Register as Freelancer with File Uploads
### ============================================
### Freelancer registration requires additional fields: specificationId and skills
### Note: profilePicture is optional, identityPicture is required

POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register/freelancer
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Jane Smith",
  "phone": "+1234567891",
  "country": "United States",
  "jobTitle": "Full Stack Developer",
  "overview": "Full stack developer specializing in React and Node.js",
  "specificationId": "specification-uuid-here",
  "skills": [
    "skill-uuid-1",
    "skill-uuid-2"
  ],
  "profilePicture": [
    {
      "fileId": "uuid-from-step-1-file-id",
      "token": "token-from-step-1-upload-token",
      "purpose": "profile"
    }
  ],
  "identityPicture": [
    {
      "fileId": "uuid-from-step-3-file-id",
      "token": "token-from-step-3-upload-token",
      "purpose": "identity",
      "fileName": "identity-front.jpg"
    }
  ],
  "previousWorks": [
    {
      "name": "E-commerce Platform",
      "description": "Built a full-featured e-commerce platform with React and Node.js",
      "link": "https://example.com/project",
      "image": "https://example.com/image.jpg",
      "gallery": [
        "https://example.com/gallery1.jpg",
        "https://example.com/gallery2.jpg"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Freelancer registered successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "user": {
###       "id": "user-uuid",
###       "name": "Jane Smith",
###       "country": "United States",
###       "jobTitle": "Full Stack Developer",
###       "overview": "Full stack developer specializing in React and Node.js",
###       "phone": "+1234567891",
###       "mode": "freelancer",
###       "skills": ["skill-uuid-1", "skill-uuid-2"],
###       "specificationId": "specification-uuid-here",
###       "profilePicture": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/profile/...",
###       "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###     },
###     "wallet": {
###       "id": "wallet-uuid",
###       "userId": "user-uuid",
###       "balance": 0,
###       "currency": "USD"
###     },
###     "identity": {
###       "id": "identity-uuid",
###       "userId": "user-uuid",
###       "isVerified": false,
###       "images": ["https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/identity/..."]
###     },
###     "portfolio": {
###       "id": "portfolio-uuid",
###       "userId": "user-uuid",
###       "previousWorks": []
###     },
###     "previousWorks": [...]
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### NOTES:
### ============================================
### 1. File Upload Flow:
###    - Step 1: Get upload URL from /api/s3/upload-url (returns fileId, uploadUrl, uploadToken)
###    - Step 2: Upload file directly to S3 using the signed uploadUrl (PUT request to S3, not our API)
###    - Step 3: Use the fileId, token, and purpose in the registration request
###    - The file reference format must be: [{ fileId: "...", token: "...", purpose: "..." }]
###    - Files must be uploaded to S3 before they can be used in registration
###
### 2. File Purposes:
###    - "profile" - For profile pictures
###    - "identity" - For identity verification documents
###
### 3. File Types:
###    - "image" - For images (jpg, png, etc.)
###    - "document" - For documents (pdf, doc, etc.)
###    - "video" - For videos
###    - "audio" - For audio files
###    - "other" - For other file types
###
### 4. Required Fields:
###    Client Registration:
###    - name, phone, country, jobTitle, overview, identityPicture
###    - profilePicture is optional
###
###    Freelancer Registration:
###    - name, phone, jobTitle, overview, specificationId, skills, identityPicture
###    - country and profilePicture are optional
###    - previousWorks is optional
###
### 5. File Reference Format:
###    - profilePicture: Array format [{ fileId, token, purpose }] (optional, max 1 item)
###    - identityPicture: Array format [{ fileId, token, purpose }] (required, min 1 item)
###    - The "purpose" field is REQUIRED and must match: "profile" or "identity"
###    - Both fields must be arrays, even for single files
###
### 6. Upload Token:
###    - Each upload URL comes with an uploadToken
###    - This token MUST be included in the registration request
###    - Tokens are stored in Valkey/Redis with TTL (default: 20 minutes)
###    - Tokens are single-use only (consumed after successful registration)
###    - Token must match the fileId and purpose exactly
###
### 7. File Status:
###    - Files are created with status "uploading" when upload URL is generated
###    - After uploading to S3, the file should have a URL set
###    - The middleware validates that file has a URL and is not "failed"
###    - Files are automatically linked to the user after successful registration
